        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah's climate, a standard asphalt shingle roof lasts about 20 to 28 years. Lifespans vary widely by material: architectural shingles last 22 to 30 years, metal roofs last 40 to 70 years, and concrete or clay tile roofs can last 50 to 100 years.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "20 to 28 years"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
