          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What Affects Roof Lifespan in Utah?"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Intense UV Exposure: High-altitude sun breaks down asphalt and granules faster than in lower-elevation states."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Temperature Swings: Utah's hot summers and freezing winters cause materials to expand and contract repeatedly."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Ice: Heavy winter snow loads and ice dams strain roof structures and flashings."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Attic Ventilation: Poor ventilation traps summer heat and winter moisture, cooking or rotting the roof deck from underneath."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Wind and Hail: Mountain storms and high wind corridors (such as areas near the Wasatch Front) can tear or lift aging shingles.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know what type of roofing material you currently have and how old it is, and I can help you spot signs of wear or figure out if an inspection is needed."
      }
